    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac660cb0_d128ff31",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/anx74xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 158,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-04T20:37:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there is a requirement on board_set_tcpc_power_mode. It is handled by the calls in usb_pd_protocol.c:\ntcpm_set_drp_toggle calls anx74xx_set_power_mode\n\nrequest_low_power_mode defers call to enter_low_power_mode by PD_LM_DEBOUCE_US and hence the delay.\n\nBut, I am worried about the fact that we could potentially end up changing the value of PD_LM_DEBOUNCE_US in the future breaking this driver. Can we leave the mdelay(1) in here so that the driver does not rely on the delay used by the usb_pd_protocol layer?",
      "parentUuid": "601b4375_2acd9332",
      "revId": "859f09bb4fdd84de89bf39a8f03ca54d9880d00b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
